      "title": "Listening to User Input",
      "sourceHash": "a4c9a1b2b48730a784a6ed64672ec584351bf0f9b13ce2c2e2557472e0cdd12d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.066,
          "end": 5.333,
          "en": "Maximilian: So let's now work on gathering user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.333,
          "end": 7.333,
          "en": "And as I said, for a start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.333,
          "end": 11.266,
          "en": "I wanna react to every change in any of the inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.266,
          "end": 13.633,
          "en": "So for example, on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.633,
          "end": 17.733,
          "en": "and I simply wanna get the value the user entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.733,
          "end": 20.833,
          "en": "and store that somewhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.833,
          "end": 21.3,
          "en": "and store that somewhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.3,
          "end": 24.2,
          "en": "And for example just log it to the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.2,
          "end": 26.533,
          "en": "Now to do that, for a start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.533,
          "end": 28.766,
          "en": "we need to add listeners to listen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.766,
          "end": 32.9,
          "en": "for every keystroke or for every change of these inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.9,
          "end": 33.133,
          "en": "for every keystroke or for every change of these inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.133,
          "end": 35.233,
          "en": "And you'll learn that you can do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.233,
          "end": 37.3,
          "en": "on the element where you wanna add a listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.3,
          "end": 39.5,
          "en": "So for example, on this input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.5,
          "end": 42.3,
          "en": "by adding a prop that starts with \"on\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 44.033,
          "en": "and then the question just is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.033,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "to which event you want to listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 47.266,
          "en": "to which event you want to listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.266,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "Now we could listen to on input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 53.166,
          "en": "and therefore react to basically every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.166,
          "end": 55.033,
          "en": "but there also is the just the on change event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.033,
          "end": 57.366,
          "en": "which basically does the same here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.366,
          "end": 59.9,
          "en": "It will also trigger on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.9,
          "end": 60.2,
          "en": "It will also trigger on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 60.2,
          "end": 62.233,
          "en": "but the advantage of the on change event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 62.233,
          "end": 63.5,
          "en": "is that we can for example",
